    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/EF/2026/Jul/ef_ap_pt_2026-07-23.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer for Master of Science in Financial Technology Management",
      "description": "Part-time Lecturer for Master of Science in Financial Technology Management \n \nThe Department of Economics and Finance invites applications for a Part‑time \nLecturer to teach in the Master of Science in Financial Technology Management \nprogramme, commencing in September 2026. The appointed candidate will be \nresponsible for delivering the following two courses: \nFINT591 Economics and Finance for FinTech \nFINT592 Cryptography and Blockchain \n \nIn addition, the candidate will be assigned to teach one course from the following list: \nFINT 502    Financial Big Data Analytics \nFINT 503    WealthTech and InsurTech \nFINT 504    RegTech and Cybersecurity \n \nRequirements \n1. A master’s degree or above in a) FinTech b) Finance / Business Administration \n(with an IT degree), or c) Computer Science / Data Science (with a Finance \ndegree), or d) a closely related discipline. Relevant professional qualifications \nwill be a plus. \n2. Relevant industry, managerial, and data handling experience in Computer \nScience, Information Technology, or FinTech. \n3. Strong communication skills and the ability to engage students effectively in \nboth theoretical and practical learning. \n \nApplication Procedure:  \nApplicants should send a letter of application together with a completed application \nform, curriculum vitae, copies of qualification documents, and three reference letters \n(recruit_ap@hksyu.edu).  \n \nFor further information about the University and the Department of Economics and \nFinance, please email Prof Rita Li (ymli@hksyu.edu). \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data collected will be used for \nstaff recruitment purposes only. The post(s) are open until filled. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/JC/2026/May/jc_ap_digicomm_ft_2026-05-27.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Academic Position in Digital Communication",
      "description": "Full-time Academic Position in Digital Communication \nDepartment of Journalism and Communication, Hong Kong Shue Yan University \n \nThe Department of Journalism and Communication is inviting applications for the post \nof Full-time Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Associate Professor of Practice / \nProfessor of Practice / Professor in Digital Communication.  \n \nRank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Candidates of Assistant \nProfessor/Associate Professor/Professor should have a doctorate degree in \ncommunication or a related discipline . Recognized professionals with substantial years \nof experience who have made significant contributions to the professional field in terms \nof practice and education of the profession could be considered as Associate Professor \nof Practice / Professor of Practice.  \n \nCandidates should demonstrate abilities to teach effectively at the undergraduate level \nwhile pursuing an active research agenda in at least one, but preferably more of the \nfollowing areas: \n1. Digital advertising  \n2. Digital public relations  \n3. Digital media communication \n \nPreference will be given to applicants with substantial tertiary-level teaching experience \nand an established track record in research and publication. The c apability of teaching \nhands-on skills using artificial intelligence and/or digital technology is also an advantage. \n \nThe appointment is contract-based, commencing in Academic Year 2026/27 and \nrenewable upon mutual agreement. \n \nApplication Procedure: \nApplicants should apply by sending: \n(1) a cover letter; \n(2) a statement of teaching and research; \n(3) a complete CV (including a list of publications); \n(4) three representative publications; \n(5) three references to be sent directly from the referees; and \n(6) the application form which can be downloaded from : \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nPlease submit your application by send ing the required documents to  University \nSecretary via email recruit_ap@hksyu.edu. \nFor further information about the Department, please visit https://jc.hksyu.edu/en. \n \nApplication Deadline: \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted.  Personal data collected will be used for \nstaff recruitment purposes only. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/BA/2024/Aug/ba_ap_pt_ft_2024-08-12.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time /Part-time Academic Position in Business Administration",
      "description": "Full-time /Part-time Academic Position in Business Administration \nDepartment of Business Administration \nThe Department of Business Administration invites applications for full - time/part-time \nLecturer/Senior Lecturer/Assistant Professor/Associate  Professor/Professor . \nApplicants should possess doctoral/master qualifications in relevant business discipline. \nFields of specialization include, but are not limited to human resource management, \ndigital marketing, applied business psychology, AI/IT business application s , and  \nbusiness analytics. \nApplicants should have a good command of both written and spoken English and \nChinese. Excellent communication skills and the ability to use Putonghua and \nSimplified Chinese as the primary language of instruction will be highly advantageous. \nPreference will also be given to those applicants who have at least two years of teaching \nexperience, a good track record in research and publication, and good academic and/or \nprofessional experience in teaching at the higher education level (bachelor and/or \nmaster). \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable upon mutual agreement. Salary will \nbe commensurate with qualifications and experience. \nApplication Procedure \nApplicants should apply by sending: \n(1) a cover letter; \n(2) a s tatement of teaching and research; \n(3) a complete CV ( including  a  list of publications); \n(4) at least two representative publications (within recent 5 years); \n(5) three references to be sent directly from the referees; and \n(6) the application form which can be downloaded from \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \nPlease send the above documents to the University Secretary via email \nrecruit_ap@hksyu.edu . For further information about the Department, please visit \nhttps://ba.hksyu.edu/. \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for \nrecruitment purposes only. The posts  are open until filled and all applications will \nreceive full consideration.  \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SOC/2026/Jul/soc_ap_ft_2026-07-03.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Assistant Professor/Associate Professor in Smart Cultural Tourism",
      "description": "Full-time Assistant Professor/Associate Professor in Smart Cultural Tourism \n(Ref: SCT 2026-06-29) \n(Start date: September 2026) \n \nHong Kong Shue Yan University invites applications for three full-time academic positions \nfor its new Master of Social Sciences in Smart Cultural Tourism (MSSc-SCT) programme, \nhosted by the Department of Sociology. The appointment will commence in September \n2026. Rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualiﬁcations and experience. \n \nThe MSSc-SCT programme is a pioneering taught postgraduate programme in Hong Kong \nthat uniquely integrates cultural tourism with smart technologies. It is strategically \ndeveloped to align with the city’s vision of becoming a smart city and a cultural hub, \nresponding to the growing industry demand for professionals who can create in-depth, \ntechnology-enhanced cultural experiences. \n \nResponsibilities: \nThe appointee will be expected to: \n• Teach postgraduate courses in the MSSc-SCT programme. \n• Supervise students’ master projects and research-informed studio work. \n• Contribute to the ongoing curriculum development and quality assurance of the \nprogramme. \n• Pursue an active research agenda, secure competitive research grants, and publish \nin high-quality refereed journals. \n• Engage in departmental and university service and administration. \n \nQualiﬁcations and Requirements: \nCandidates should possess: \n• A doctoral degree from a recognised university in a relevant ﬁeld (e.g., digital \nheritage, digital humanities, or cultural computing). \n• Demonstrated expertise or a strong research track record in conducting \ninterdisciplinary research at the intersection of cultural/heritage tourism and digital \ntechnologies (e.g., AR, VR, MR). \n• Relevant teaching experience in smart cultural tourism or closely related \ndisciplines. \n• High proﬁciency in both English and Chinese (Putonghua), with the ability to teach \neffectively across the programme’s dual-language streams. \n• Relevant industry work experience or a strong professional industry network is \nhighly preferred. \n \nThe Programme: \nThe Master of Social Sciences in Smart Cultural Tourism (MSSc-SCT) is an innovative, \ninterdisciplinary programme designed to cultivate professionals who can transform \ncultural content into engaging tourism experiences enhanced by smart technologies (e.g., \nAI, VR/AR, interactive media). The curriculum is built on two foundations: Domain \nKnowledge of Cultural Tourism and Smart Technology Application Skills, preparing \ngraduates for diverse careers in the tourism, cultural, creative, and technology sectors. \n \nApplication Procedure: \nApplications should be sent via email to recruit_ap@hksyu.edu and must include the \nfollowing documents: \n1. A cover letter \n2. A completed application form (please click here to download) \n3. A full CV (including a detailed list of research projects and publications) \n4. A teaching statement (max. 250 words) \n5. A research statement (max. 250 words) \n6. Two representative publications \n7. Three reference letters (please arrange for the referees to send the letters directly to \nthe application email address) \n \nFor enquiries about the positions, please send an email to Dr. Shengdan CAI at \nscai@hksyu.edu. \n \nClosing Date: Review of applications will commence on 15 July 2026 and will continue \nuntil the position is ﬁlled. \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. The personal data received will be kept \nconﬁdential and used for recruitment purposes only. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/May/counpsy_ap_ft_2026-05-28.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Academic Position in Counselling Psychology",
      "description": "Full-time Academic Position in Counselling Psychology \n \nDepartment of Counselling and Psychology \nThe Department of Counselling and Psychology invites applications for full-time \nacademic positions. Applicants should hold a doctoral degree in Psychology or a related \nfield, along with relevant teaching and research experience. Experience in at least one, \npreferably more, of the following areas would be advantageous: \n Criminal Psychology \n Forensic Psychology \n Investigative Psychology \n Play Therapy \n Trauma Psychology \n Sport Psychology \n Psychology of Exercise \n Industrial and Organisational Psychology \n Physical Therapy \nThe appointees are expected to provide research supervision to students at \nundergraduate and postgraduate levels. The academic rank offered will be \ncommensurate with the academic and/or clinical background and experience of the \nsuccessful candidate.  \n \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable upon mutual agreement.  \n \nFurther details of the Department and its programmes are located at \nhttp://www.hksyu.edu/counpsy/. \n \nApplication Procedure \nApplicants should send a letter of application together with a completed application \nform, curriculum vitae, copies of qualification documents, three reference letters from \npeople who know your work, and one sample of your most recent publications to \nrecruit_ap@hksyu.edu \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data collected will be used for \nstaff recruitment purposes only. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Eng/2025/Feb/eng_lc_ft_2025-02-18.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Lecturer/Senior Lecturer Positions",
      "description": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University \nDepartment of English Language and Literature \nFull-time Lecturer/Senior Lecturer Positions \nThe Department of English Language and Literature invites applications for the posts of \nLecturer/Senior Lecturer. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in English or a related subject and \ndemonstrated ability to teach academic literacy and general English language skills effectively \nat the undergraduate level. Preference will be given to applicants with at least two years’ tertiary \nlevel teaching experience.  \nLecturers will be expected to teach 18 hours per week and undertake research as well as \nundertaking administrative duties as assigned by the Department Head. \nSuitably qualified and experienced applicants could be considered for appointment at the rank \nof Senior Lecturer. \nThe application should contain a cover letter, a complete CV, a completed application form \n(available at the External Vacancies section of the University website at https://\nwww.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy) and three references  to be sent directly from \nthe referees to University Secretary via email recruit_ap@hksyu.edu. \nFor further information about the University please visit https://www.hksyu.edu/en/ and the \nDepartment of English Language and Literature website at https://english.hksyu.edu/. \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for \nrecruitment purposes only.  \nThe position will remain open until filled. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Eng/2025/Feb/eng_ap_ft_2025-02-18.pdf": {
      "title": "Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University \nDepartment of English Language and Literature \nProfessor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor \nThe Department of English Language and Literature invites applications for the post \nof full-ti me Professor, Associate or Assistant Professor. Rank will be \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. Candidates  should have a \ndoctoral degree in English specializing in literature, linguistics or a related \nfield and demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and \npostgraduate levels while pursuing an active research agenda. Preference will be \ngiven to candidates with experience in research postgraduate supervision. \nSuccessful candidates may also be asked to contribute to the teaching of academic \nliteracy. Preference will be given to applicants with substantial tertiary level teaching \nexperience a nd an established t rack record in research a nd publication.  \nApplications  should  be addressed  to: The University Secretary , Hong Kong Shue Yan \nUniversity, 10 Wai Tsui Crescent, Braemar Hill, North Point, Hong Kong and sent by \nemail to recruit_ap@hksyu.edu. The application  should  contain  a cover letter, a \ncomplete  CV including  a list of publications, two representative  publications,  a \ncompleted  application  form (available  at the External  Vacancies  section  of the \nUniversity  website  at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external- vacancy ) and three \nreferences  to be sent directly  from the referees.   \nFor further information about   the University , please visit https://www.hksyu.edu/en/ \nand the Department of English Language and Literature website at \nhttps://english.hksyu.edu/. \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used \nfor recruitment purposes only. \nApplications should be submitted as soon as possible.   The position will remain open \nuntil filled. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Eng/2025/Jun/eng_lc_pt_2025-06-30.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer positions",
      "description": "June 2025  \nHong Kong Shue Yan University \nDepartment of English Language and Literature \n \nPart-time Lecturer positions \n \nThe Department of English Language and Literature invites applications for the posts of part- \ntime Lecturer. Applicants should have a recognized degree in English or a related subject and \ndemonstrated ability to teach academic literacy and general English language skills effectively \nat the undergraduate level. Preference will be given to applicants with a higher degree in \nEnglish or a related subject and at least two years’ tertiary level teaching experience. \n \nThe application should contain a cover letter, a complete CV, and three references to be sent \ndirectly from the referees. The application may be submitted by email to english@hksyu.edu. \n \nFor further information about the University please visit https://www.hksyu.edu/en/ and the \nDepartment of English Language and Literature website https://english.hksyu.edu/. For other \nenquiries, please email english@hksyu.edu. \n \n \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for \nrecruitment purposes only. \n \nApplications should be submitted as soon as possible. \nThe positions will remain open until filled. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SW/2026/Apr/ap_sw_fs_pt_2026-04-08.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-Time Fieldwork Supervisor",
      "description": "Part-Time Fieldwork Supervisor \n \nDepartment of Social Work is inviting applications for part-time Fieldwork Supervisor.  \n \nKey Responsibilities: \nThe successful candidate will be tasked with the following duties:  \n(i) Supervising social work students during their fieldwork placements;  \n(ii) Evaluating and grading students' assignments, as well as preparing \nsupervision records and related documentation;  \n(iii) Participating in meetings and trainings. \n \nQualifications: \nCandidates must satisfy the following criteria:  \n(i) Hold a recognized degree in social work and/or possession of a postgraduate \ndegree in social work or a related discipline;  \n(ii) Possess at least five years of full-time-equivalent post-degree professional \npractice experience (at a rank equivalent to ASWO); \n(iii) Demonstrate strong communication and interpersonal skills; \n(iv) Possess strong written and spoken English and Chinese skills. \n \nPlease note that we will conduct a short Zoom interview before the start of each annual \nplacement. These interviews are normally held between March and April and between \nJune and July. \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable by mutual agreement for each \ncohort. Enquiries and applications should be sent to the Fieldwork Team at \nswfw_joint@hksyu.edu.  \nPlease indicate your supervision preference priority (e.g., 1st: BSW, \n2nd: MSW or vice versa) in both the email subject line and your CV. \nApplication Deadline \nUntil the position is filled \n \nPosting date: 8 April 2026 "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SW/2024/Apr/sw_coord_l_sl_pt_ft_2024-04-02.pdf": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer / Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer / Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor \nDepartment of Social Work \n \nDepartment of Social Work is inviting applications for full -time Lecturer, Senior \nLecturer, Assistant Professor , Associate Professor  and Professor. Rank will \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \n Requirements for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer: \nCandidates should have a master degree in social work or related disciplines, and \n5 years of clinical practice experience as a social worker. Preference will be given \nto applicants with at least two years of teaching experience at the undergraduate \nlevel and conducting fieldwork supervision. Applicants are expected to take up \nteaching task, fieldwork supervision and administrating task. \n \nApplications should contain (a) application form, (b) a cover letter, and (c) a \ncomplete CV. \n \n Requirements for Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor: \nCandidates should have a doctorate degree in social work or related disciplines, \nand 5 years of clinical practice experience as a social worker. Preference will be \ngiven to applicants with at least two years of teaching experience at the \nundergraduate and postgraduate levels and a good track record in research and \npublication. Applicants are expected to pursue an active research agenda. \n \nFields of specialization could include, but not limited to, children and family; \nyouth work; digital social work practice; support for children with special needs; \nsocial service management; interdisciplinary collaboration; social policy and \nadvocacy. Proficiency in Chinese and English is required. \n \nApplications should contain (a) application form, (b) a cover letter, (c) a complete \nCV including list of publications, ( d) a sample of recent publications, and ( e) 3 \nreferences to be sent directly from the referees to the Executive Officer.  \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable upon mutual agreement. \n \nEnquiry and application should be sent to the University Secretary at \nrecruit_ap@hksyu.edu. \n \nApplication Deadline \nDeadline: Open Until Filled \n \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal  data collected will be used for \nstaff recruitment purpose only. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/qess/2026/Jul/qess_ro_ft_2026-07-15.pdf": {
      "title": "Project Officer",
      "description": "Project Officer  \nHong Kong Shue Yan University is seeking a high-calibre Project Officer for the QESS-\nfunded project titled “Enhancing Students’ Emotional Wellness and Resilience in Post-\nsecondary Institutions.” This initiative aims to strengthen student mental wellness and \nresilience through a multi-pronged approach featuring a dedicated online learning platform, \nan AI-powered consultation chatbot, and experiential wellness programs. \nMajor Duties & Responsibilities \n• Plan, implement, and monitor project activities to ensure timely, high-quality execution in \nline with milestones. \n• Design and conduct project evaluation studies, including survey design, data collection, \nrigorous data analysis, and reporting. \n• Prepare comprehensive progress reports, engaging presentations, and concise evaluation \nsummaries for stakeholders. \n• Organize and facilitate workshops, seminars, committee meetings, and training events to \nsupport project objectives. \n• Support student-led activities and oversee the Student Ambassador Program to promote \nmental wellness and resilience on campus. \n• Develop and design creative promotional materials, including posters, infographics, and \nengaging content for social media platforms. \n• Regularly update and maintain the project website and online learning platform to ensure \ncontent is current and accurate. \n• Act as a key point of contact to maintain seamless communication with partner \ninstitutions, external collaborators, Student Ambassadors, and technical vendors. \n• Maintain meticulous project documentation, track budgets, and prepare progress reports \nin compliance with funding and organizational standards. \nQualifications & Requirements \n• A Bachelor’s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, IT \nManagement, or a related discipline. \n• Proven experience in project coordination, survey design, and data collection/analysis is \nhighly preferred. \n• Strong organizational, administrative, and interpersonal communication skills. \n• Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese). \n• A genuine passion for promoting student mental health, resilience, and well-being. \nApplication  \nInterested applicants should submit a completed application form (specifying expected \nsalary), alongside a cover letter and an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Dr Jason CHOW \n(tschow@hksyu.edu). The official application form can be downloaded at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \nAll applications will be treated in strict confidence. Only shortlisted candidates will be \ncontacted. \nClosing Date: by 10 August 2026 or until the position is filled.   "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Jul/counpsy_pa_ft_2026-07-10.pdf": {
      "title": "Job Title: Project Assistant [1 position]",
      "description": "Job Title: Project Assistant [1 position] \nMode: Full-time \nAppointment Period: 4-5 months with the possibility of renewal subject to mutual agreement \nDepartment: Department of Counselling & Psychology (Brain Stimulation Laboratory) \nClosing Date: August 31st 2026 \n \n(1) Project Assistant  \nJob Duties \nThe appointee will be responsible for (a) conducting quantitative and qualitative research studies, \nincluding research design, data collection, analysis, compilation of reports and other \nforms of deliverables; (b) providing administrative support to the director (Dr. Bess Lam); (c) \nPreparing literature review regarding neuroscience and psychology; (d) compiling progress reports \nand the final report; e) assisting the publications and other related research work in the laboratory; and \nf) maintaining laboratory equipment and ensure compliance with safety protocols. Supportive \nsupervision will be provided upon appointment. \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should have \n(a) bachelor’s degree in Psychology or a related field; \n(b) excellent command of SPSS; \n(c) good skills in psychology- related data collection; \n(d) excellent command of English and Chinese language (Cantonese); \n(e) personal quality of good responsibility, industriousness and readiness to learn and to help other \npeople. \n \n \nFunding information \nThe post is funded by private donation by Save the Children (Hong Kong). Salary will be \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience.  \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter, and a curriculum \nvitae (CV) to: Dr. Bess Lam at Email yhlam@hksyu.edu with the subject “application for \nproject assistant”. It would be nice if the applicant could also attach to the email a sample of his or her \nuniversity assignments or research papers that can demonstrate his or her proficiency in English \nwriting. Application forms can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/tc/about/career/ \nAll applicants will be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/OAVP/2026/May/oavp_ea_ft_2026-05-27.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Full-time Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant I, Office of the",
      "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nPosition: Full-time Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant I, Office of the \nAcademic Vice President  \n \nResponsibilities \n To provide high-level administrative and secretarial support for the daily office operations, \nmeetings, committees, and events; \n To coordinate meeting logistics, prepare agendas and papers, and produce accurate \nmeeting minutes; \n To draft, review, and handle confidential correspondence, reports, and presentations; \n To liaise with faculties, departments, and administrative units on academic matters and \nsubmissions; \n To manage an effective filing system and database for records; \n To provide assistance on University functions as required (e.g. Luncheon meeting; Staff \nForum); \n To perform any other duties as assigned by the Academic Vice President.  \n \nRequirements \n Bachelor’s degree holder; \n Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; \n Possess initiative in handling different tasks with tight timelines; \n Be able to work independently and efficiently in a fast-paced environment; \n A team player with good interpersonal and communication skills; \n Knowledge in basic webpage management skills and design preferred; \n Salary will be commensurate with qualification and experience. \n \nCandidates with more relevant experience may be considered for appointment as Senior \nExecutive Assistant. \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form and resume to the Academic Vice President \n(via email: tytwong@hksyu.edu). The application form can be obtained at:  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc  \n \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/APDO/2026/May/apdo_eo_ft_2026-05-18.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Executive Officer, Accreditation and Programme Development Office (APDO)",
      "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \n \nPosition: Executive Officer, Accreditation and Programme Development Office (APDO) \n \nResponsibilities \n To provide administrative and secretarial support for accreditation exercises; \n To support the administration of the University’s QA mechanisms and initiatives; \n Secretarial work on committees; \n To conduct surveys and feedback exercises to support programme review and development; \n To liaise with academic and administrative departments of the University  in preparation for \nprogramme review and development; \n To provide assistance for University functions as required (e.g. graduation ceremony, academic \nevents, recruitment exercise, etc). \n To perform any other duties as assigned by the Head / Supervisor \n \n \nRequirements \n Bachelor’s degree holder, with 4 years or more of relevant post qualification working experience \npreferred \n Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (ability to edit documents will \nbe an advantage) \n Possess initiative in handling different tasks with tight timelines \n Be able to work independently and efficiently in a fast-paced environment \n A team player with good interpersonal and communication skills \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form and a curriculum vitae (CV) with the \nexpected salary to the Registrar at reg_recruit@hksyu.edu .   \n \nApplication Deadline: until the post is filled.  \n \nThe application form can be downloaded at  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/download/Application%20Form%20for%20non-Academic%20Positions.doc \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/UAO/2026/Jun/uao_ao_marketing_ft_2026-06-30.pdf": {
      "title": "Admissions Oﬃcer (Marke�ng and Admissions)",
      "description": "Admissions Oﬃcer (Marke�ng and Admissions) \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, Registry   \nUniversity Admissions Oﬃce   \nWe are seeking a dynamic, digitally savvy, and highly organized professional to join our team. \nWhile this role sits within the Admissions Oﬃce, the primary focus is to drive the university’s \ndigital transforma�on and brand presence. You will play a pivotal role in leading our website \nrevamp projects and execu�ng comprehensive marke�ng campaigns to engage prospec�ve \nlocal, mainland, and overseas students. \nCore Responsibili�es: \n1. Lead Website Revamp Projects: Take full ownership of website revamps. Manage \nend-to-end project lifecycles with internal and external stakeholders, u�lizing strong \nexperience in UX/UI design, data migra�on, SEO, and web analy�cs (e.g., GA4). \n2. Drive Digital Marke�ng Strategy: Develop and oversee a comprehensive digital \nmarke�ng strategy. Create engaging content across key social media pla�orms, \norchestrate email newsleters, and launch targeted online campaigns to enhance \nprogramme visibility. \n3. End-to-End Campaign Management: Manage mul�media marke�ng projects from \nconcept to comple�on, including video produc�on, online/oﬄine adver�sing, and \ncon�nuous website management to eﬀec�vely promote the university's oﬀerings. \n4. Event Coordina�on: Event-manage a diverse calendar of promo�onal ac�vi�es, \nincluding admissions seminars, Informa�on Day, school visits, and educa�on expos \nto atract qualiﬁed applicants. \n5. Admissions Support: Provide administra�ve support to the core admissions team, \nincluding handling student enquiries and processing applica�ons during peak cycles. \nKey Requirements: \n• A bachelor’s degree in marke�ng, communica�ons, crea�ve/web design or a related \nﬁeld at least 3 years’ relevant experience. \n• Proven experience in web design project management and digital marke�ng best \nprac�ces is mandatory. Technical knowledge of web development is a strong plus. \n• Knowledge in digital graphic or video content crea�on using industry tools (e.g., \nAdobe Illustrator/Photoshop/Canva or Adobe Premiere/A�er Eﬀects/CapCut) is \nhighly advantageous. \n• Fluency in English, Cantonese, and Mandarin, with excep�onal communica�on skills \nfor both professional wri�ng and dynamic presenta�ons. \n• Strong organiza�onal skills with the ability to manage mul�ple projects \nsimultaneously in a fast-paced environment. \n \nApplica�on Methods:   \n1) Applicants should send a cover leter, an applica�on form and a curriculum vitae (CV) with \nexpected salary to the Director of University Admissions Oﬃce at newapp@hksyu.edu; \n2) Applica�on form can be downloaded \nat: htps://www.hksyu.edu/download/Applica�on%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Posi�ons.doc  \nReview of applica�ons will start as soon as possible and con�nue un�l the post is ﬁlled.   \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/UAO/2026/Jun/uao_ao_media_ft_2026-06-30.pdf": {
      "title": "Admissions Oﬃcer (Mul�media Produc�on)",
      "description": "Admissions Oﬃcer (Mul�media Produc�on) \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, Registry   \nUniversity Admissions Oﬃce   \nWe are seeking a dynamic, crea�ve, and highly skilled mul�media professional to join our \nteam. While this role oﬃcially sits within the Admissions Oﬃce, the primary focus is high-\nquality video edi�ng and produc�on. You will play a pivotal role in crea�ng engaging visual \nstorytelling aimed at promo�ng our university and programmes to local, mainland, and \noverseas students. \nCore Responsibili�es: \n1. Mul�media Content Crea�on: Design and produce engaging mul�media and video \ncontent that aligns with current digital trends and marke�ng insights. Tailor content \nspeciﬁcally for the university website, YouTube channel, and major social media \npla�orms (including Facebook, Instagram, WeChat, and Xiaohongshu). \n2. Post-Produc�on & Edi�ng: Master the edi�ng and post-produc�on workﬂow to \nensure top-�er visual quality, expertly incorpora�ng music, sound design, color \ngrading, and visual eﬀects (VFX) as needed. \n3. Video & Photo Shoo�ng: Execute high-quality video produc�on from concept to \nwrap; hands-on experience in professional photography and photo shoo�ng is a \nstrong plus. \n4. Team Collabora�on: Collaborate closely with internal academic and administra�ve \nteams to ensure brand consistency, narra�ve alignment, and �mely delivery of \ncontent. \n5. Event & Campaign Support: Support various admission events (e.g., Info Day, \neduca�on expos, school visits) and par�cipate in ad-hoc promo�onal projects to \nelevate the university's public proﬁle. \nKey Requirements: \n• Higher diploma or degree in Film & Media, Crea�ve Media, Adver�sing, Marke�ng, \nor related ﬁeld with a minimum of 2-3 years of relevant experience in video \nproduc�on. \n• Proﬁcient in professional video edi�ng and mo�on graphics using Adobe Premiere \nand A�er Eﬀects. \n• Proﬁcient with video produc�on equipment (cameras, ligh�ng setups and audio gear \netc) across pre-produc�on, shoo�ng and ligh�ng.  \n• Familiarity with graphic design, sound produc�on, and/or 3D anima�on is an \nadvantage. \n• Submission of a por�olio or showreel is mandatory. Please include valid link(s) in \nyour cover leter or applica�on form.  \n• Fluent in writen and spoken English, Cantonese and Mandarin. \n \nApplica�on Methods:   \n1) Applicants should send a cover leter, an applica�on form and a curriculum vitae (CV) with \nexpected salary to the Director of University Admissions Oﬃce at newapp@hksyu.edu; \n2) Applica�on form can be downloaded \nat: htps://www.hksyu.edu/download/Applica�on%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Posi�ons.doc  \nReview of applica�ons will start as soon as possible and con�nue un�l the post is ﬁlled.   \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CIEBPR/2026/Jul/ciebpr_pm_po_ft_2026-07-14.pdf": {
      "title": "Mrs. Dorothy Koo and Dr. Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and",
      "description": "Mrs. Dorothy Koo and Dr. Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and \nResearch of the Hong Kong Shue Yan University \n \nProject Manager/Project Officer  \n \nResponsibilities: \n• Develop and maintain project timelines and budgets. \n• Coordinate with stakeholders to ensure the successful development and delivery of the training \nprogram, and publicity events  \n• Manage the project website and other publicity channels. \n• Assist the project leaders to draft the progress, evaluation, and completion report \n• Any other responsibilities as assigned by the Centre Directors \n \nRequirements:  \n• Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 3 years of project management experience for Project \nManager, and 1 years for Project Officer \n• Experience in managing large-scale education projects is preferred.  \n• Strong leadership, communication and problem-solving skills. \n• Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n• Familiarity with website and social media management preferred. \n \nApplication  \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter and \nan updated curriculum vitae to the Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary \nEvidence-based Practice & Research (ciebpr@hksyu.edu). Application form (research positions) can be \ndownloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in strict confidence. \nOnly those who are shortlisted will be contacted. Closing Date: by July 31 or until position is filled. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CIEBPR/2026/Mar/ciepbr_po_eo_ft_2026-03-30.pdf": {
      "title": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice",
      "description": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice \nand Research \n \nHong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) \n \nProject Officer / Executive Officer \n \nThe Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) is seeking high-calibre candidates to join the Mrs \nDorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and \nResearch.  The Centre hosts a community project that aspires to strengthen the social-emotional \ncapabilities of students and their parents, teachers, social workers, and the public.  The project \nincorporates gamification elements into social-emotional learning programmes for Primary 3 and 4 \nstudents. \n \nResponsibilities: \n To provide administrative, clerical, financial, and operational support for the abovementioned \nproject; \n To gather and maintain proper documentation and records; \n To support evaluation and research studies; \n To liaise with internal units, external suppliers and stakeholders; \n To coordinate with the co-organizer and partner schools to facilitate the implementation of the \nproject; \n To organize events, including public education activities and training sessions; \n To assist in building the project brand, such as managing social media channels, conducting \npublicity campaigns, coordinating media interviews, drafting press releases, writing marketing \ncontent and implementing an SEO campaign; \n To support for the enhancement of a gamified e-learning platform, a mobile application, \neducational materials, animation series and videos, etc.; \n To supervise and provide guidance to student helpers; \n To perform any other duties as assigned. \n \nRequirements: \n A Bachelor’s degree in Social Sciences, Marketing, Business Administration, or related \ndiscipline; \n Preferably 2–3 years of relevant working experience; experience in the tertiary education sector \nwould be an advantage; \n Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); \n Proficiency in common office applications (e.g. MS Office Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook); \n Ability to work both independently and collaboratively with efficiency and accuracy; \n Strong organizational skill and attention to detail; \n A strong sense of responsibility. \nCandidates with less experience and will be considered.  Fresh graduates are welcome to apply.  \n \nApplication: \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover \nletter and an updated curriculum vitae, to the Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for \nInterdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice & Research (ciebpr@hksyu.edu). \n \nApplication form (non-academic posts) can be downloaded \nat: https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \n \nAll applications will be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be \ncontacted. \n \nClosing Date: 29 April 2026 or until the positions are filled, whichever is earlier. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Registry/2026/May/reg_ea_eo_ft_2026-05-27.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Full-time Executive Assistant / Executive Officer",
      "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nPosition: Full-time Executive Assistant / Executive Officer \n \nApplicants should possess  \n(i) a Bachelor’s degree with at least 1 year of work experience, preferably in the \neducation sector;  \n(ii) good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, and being able \nto communicate effectively in Putonghua;  \n(iii) self-motivative and strong sense of responsibility; \n(iv) good organizational skills, communication skills, interpersonal skills and \nanalytical abilities; \n(v) good computer skills. \n \nDuties: \n(i) provide administrative and secretarial support to the Academic Department at Registry; \n(ii) perform administrative support to academic services through registration, courses \nenrolment, tuition fee payment, assessment, graduation, management of student records, \ntestimonial and transcript issuance; \n(iii) handle written and verbal enquries; \n(iv) provide administrative support to University-wide functions such as recruitment of new \nstudents, Athletic Meet and Graduation Ceremony; and \n(v) perform any other duties assigned by the Head of Department / Supervisor. \n \nCandidates with relevant work experience in tertiary education may apply for the \nposition of Executive Officer. \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form and a curriculum vitae (CV) \nwith the expected salary to the Registrar at reg_recruit@hksyu.edu .   \n \nClosing Date: Until the post is filled \n \nThe application form can be downloaded at  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/download/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used \nsolely for recruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the \nrecruitment exercise. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/UAO/2026/Mar/uao_aa_ft_2026-03-03.pdf": {
      "title": "Admissions Assistant / Officer (Admissions Advisory",
      "description": "Admissions Assistant / Officer (Admissions Advisory \nand Administration)  \n \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, Registry  \nUniversity Admissions Office  \n \nWe are seeking a dynamic and organized Admissions Officer to join our team. You will play a \npivotal role in recruiting and supporting students from diverse backgrounds throughout the \nentire admissions journey. \n \nCore Responsibilities: \n1. Organize and manage a schedule of recruitment events locally and abroad, such as \nuniversity fairs, school visits, open days and admissions talks. \n2. Create and give presentations to prospective students and their parents and career \ncounsellors to promote the university's programmes and entry criteria. \n3. Advise prospective students on programme selection, admission requirements, \nscholarships, and the application steps. \n4. Oversee applications from start to finish, including reviewing applicant files and \nresponding to inquiries about application status. \n5. Manage the student visa process for non-local students, assisting with required \ndocuments and communicating with immigration officials. \n \nKey Requirements:  \n- A bachelor's degree. Applications from fresh graduates are welcome. \n- Excellent communication skills, with full professional proficiency and fluency \nin Cantonese and Mandarin and English. \n- Strong administrative and organizational skills, with keen attention to detail. \n- A customer-service oriented mindset, with the patience and empathy to guide prospective \nstudents. \n \nApplication Methods:  \n1)Applicants should send a cover letter and a curriculum vitae (CV) with expected salary to \nthe Director of University Admissions Office at newapp@hksyu.edu; or  \n 2)Complete the application form which can be downloaded at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc, and send it together with a CV to newapp@hksyu.edu.  \n \nSalary and Conditions of Service  \nRemuneration package will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and \nexperience. Appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract and renewable with mutual \nconsent.  \n \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. \nApplicants with less experience may be considered for the post of Admissions Assistant.   \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely \nfor recruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment \nexercise. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/HMU/2026/Feb/hmu_ssossa_ft_2026-02-02.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Student Services Officer / Student Services Assistant(Hall Management Unit)",
      "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nPosition: Student Services Officer / Student Services Assistant(Hall Management Unit) \n \nThe appointee will be responsible for supporting Hall-based Student Engagement initiatives and providing a\ndministrative and logistical support to the Hall Management Unit. \n \nMajor Responsibilities \n● Assist in the development, coordination, and implementation of hall -based student engagement pro\ngrammes; \n● Support the coaching and supervision of student leaders in programme planning and hall-related ma\ntters; \n● Manage and update promotional channels, including programme websites; design promotional mate\nrials and maintain social media platforms; \n● Provide student support services, including front desk services, handling enquiries, managing check\n-in/check-out procedures, processing payments, and preparing monthly reports; \n● Provide operational and logistical support to Warden Teams as required; \n● Knowledge of video production and editing is an advantage; \n● Perform other duties as assigned. \n \nRequirements \n● Bachelor’s degree or equivalent qualification; \n● Strong administrative abilities with excellent interpersonal skills; \n● Self-motivated, people-oriented, and with a strong sense of responsibility; \n● Demonstrated interest in and ability to handle student-related matters; \n● Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese, including Mandarin; \n● Prior working experience in student services or related fields will be an advantage. \n \nCandidates with more relevant experience may be considered for appointment as Student Services Officer. \n \nAppointment will be offered a two-years contract, with the possibility of renewal, subject to mutual agreem\nent. Application form can be obtained here. \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, resume and Cover Letter to Hall Management Unit, H\nong Kong Shue Yan University,10 Wai Tsui Crescent, Braemar Hill, North Point, H.K. or via email to tccha\nn@hksyu.edu. \n \nReview of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled.Only shortlisted app\nlicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for recruitment-related purpose. All a\npplications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/ESG/2026/Apr/esg_tomo_ft_2026-04-17.pdf": {
      "title": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) invites applications for the position of Technical",
      "description": "Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) invites applications for the position of Technical \nand Operations Manager / Officer under the Office of ESG and Sustainable \nDevelopment. The appointee will support campus development, building operation, and \nfacilities-related initiatives, with a focus on technical coordination, environmental \nperformance, and operational effectiveness across University campuses. \n \nMajor Responsibilities \n \nReporting to the Director, the appointee will be responsible for the technical and operational \naspects of campus facilities management, including but not limited to: \n \n• Supporting the planning, coordination, and implementation of ESG-related operational \ninitiatives, including energy efficiency measures, waste reduction programmes, and data \ncollection to support sustainability monitoring and institutional reporting \n• Supporting the planning, operation, and maintenance of University buildings and \nfacilities, including new campus developments and student hostel projects \n• Coordinating with the Facility Management Office on building services operation, \nmaintenance works, and facilities-related improvement initiatives \n• Conducting data collection and technical assessments related to carbon emissions, energy \nefficiency, and sustainability performance \n• Assisting in the preparation of technical reports, performance summaries, and institutional \nreports \n• Supporting the implementation of operational improvements related to building \nperformance, safety, operational effectiveness, and cost efficiency \n• Supporting procurement and contractor coordination related to facilities operation and \nmaintenance, with due consideration of sustainability criteria, life-cycle cost, and \nenvironmentally responsible practices \n• Liaising with internal units, consultants, and contractors on facilities management and \ncompliance-related matters, including environmental performance, sustainability \nrequirements, and relevant ESG-related standards \n• Performing other duties as assigned in support of campus operations and development \ninitiatives \nRequirements \nApplicants should possess: \n \n• A bachelor’s degree or above in surveying, facilities management, building services \nengineering, mechanical or electrical engineering, environmental engineering, or a related \ndiscipline \n• At least three years of solid experience in facilities management, surveying, building \nservices operation, or technical operations, preferably in large-scale institutions, public \norganisations, or tertiary education settings \n• Professional qualification as a Registered Facility Manager (RFM) or Certified Facility \nManager (CFM) \n• Corporate or Professional Membership of the Hong Kong Institute of Facility Management \n(HKIFM) will be an advantage \n• Professional Membership of the Hong Kong Institute of Surveyors (MHKIS) will be an \nadvantage \n• Sound knowledge of building services systems, including electrical, mechanical, HVAC, \nfire services, and plumbing and drainage systems \n• Familiarity with ESG-related concepts, sustainability practices, and environmental \nperformance monitoring in facilities and campus operations \n• Understanding of relevant Hong Kong ordinances, regulations, and codes of practice related \nto building services operation, facilities management, and surveying practices \n• Experience in contractor coordination, technical documentation, surveying-related works, \nand operational monitoring \n• Strong organisational, analytical, and reporting skills \n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively with academic and administrative \nstakeholders \n• Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese \n \nAppointment and Benefits \nThe appointment will be made on a contract basis, with remuneration commensurate with \nqualifications and experience. Applicants should send a completed application form with \nexpected salary, together with a cover letter and an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Ms. \nBeatrice Wong (bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application form can be downloaded at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in strict confidence. \nOnly those who are shortlisted will be contacted. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2025/Oct/rcdtbi_po_ft_2025-10-30.pdf": {
      "title": "Full Time Project Officers (Full-time)",
      "description": "Full Time Project Officers (Full-time) \nWe are hiring two Project Officers for the QESS project “Enhancing Students’ Emotional Wellness \nand Resilience in Post -secondary Institutions” under the Research Center for Digital Education and \nBlended Intelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. The project aims to enhance students’ \nemotional wellness and resilience through an online platform, AI -powered consultation chatbot, and \nexperiential wellness programs. The Project Officers will support the planning, implementation, and \nevaluation of project activities, including coordinating workshops and events, managing \ndocumentation, designing surveys and promotional materials, analysing data, updating online \nplatforms, and liaising with Student Ambassadors, partner institutions, and technical vendors. \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities  \n• Plan, implement, and monitor project activities to ensure timely and effective execution. \n• Design and conduct evaluation studies, including data collection, analysis, and reporting. \n• Prepare comprehensive reports, engaging presentations, and concise evaluation summaries to \ncommunicate project findings and progress. \n• Coordinate and facilitate workshops, meetings, seminars, and training events to support project \ngoals. \n• Support and organise student activities and oversee the Student Ambassador Program, promoting \nmental wellness and resilience. \n• Develop and design promotional materials, including posters, infographics, and content for social \nmedia platforms. \n• Update and maintain the project website and online learning platform to ensure accurate and \ncurrent information. \n• Liaise with partner institutions, external collaborators, Student Ambassadors, and technical \nvendors to foster strong relationships and ensure seamless communication. \n• Maintain project documentation, including budgets, progress reports, and other records, ensuring \ncompliance with organisational standards. \nQualifications and Requirements  \n• A Bachelor’s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, IT Management, or \nrelated disciplines. \n• Experience in data collection/analysis, survey design, and/or project coordination preferred. \n• Proficiency in design tools (e.g., Adobe Illustrator) and data analysis software (SPSS, Mplus, R) \nis an advantage. \n• Strong organizational, writing, and interpersonal skills. \n• Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n• Interest in promoting student mental health and wellness. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up- to-date curriculum vitae to Ms.  Beatrice Wong ( bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ . All applications will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 20 November 2025 or until the position is filled.   "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2025/Oct/rcdtbi_po_pm_ft_2025-10-30.pdf": {
      "title": "AI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub for the Self -Financing Higher Education Sector”  under",
      "description": "Full Time Project Officer / Project Manager  \nWe are hiring one Project Officer and one Project Manager  for the QESS project “Developing an \nAI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub for the Self -Financing Higher Education Sector”  under \nthe Research Center for Digital Education and Blended Intelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. \nThis inter-institutional project aims to identify, centralize, and utilize AI learning resources and tools \nto support teaching and the development of A I literacy among post -secondary teachers, provide \neffective AI tools for teaching in self -financing institutions, organize professional development \nactivities, and conduct research to evaluate AI literacy initiatives. \nThe Project Officer / Project Manager will lead and coordinate all aspects of the project, ensuring \ntimely completion of deliverables, smooth collaboration among teams, and effective implementation \nof the AI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub. \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n• Plan, implement, and monitor project activities, ensuring milestones are achieved on time and \nwithin budget. \n• Oversee the development and maintenance of the online AI-Enhanced Teaching Resource Hub, \nincluding functionality, accessibility, and scalability. \n• Coordinate with technical teams, faculty contributors, and subject matter experts to integrate AI \ntools, preloaded prompts, lesson planning tools, and assessment features. \n• Manage content creation and organization for the platform, including training session videos, \nteaching showcases, and self-learning materials. \n• Organize and support professional development activities such as workshops, Coffee Talk \nmeetings, and public seminars; handle registrations, promotions, and resource distribution. \n• Track platform analytics, participation data, and engagement metrics; prepare progress reports \nand final reports for stakeholders and funding bodies. \n• Liaise with partner institutions, external collaborators, technical vendors and project teams to \nensure smooth collaboration and communication. \n• Manage project documentation, budget tracking, procurement, and other administrative tasks. \nQualifications and Requirements \n• A Bachelor’s degree or above in Education, Information Technology, Psychology, Social \nSciences, or a related discipline. \n• At least 2-3 years’ experience in project management in educational or research settings. \n• Experience in liaising with technical vendors or digital project teams is an advantage. \n• Strong organizational, communication, writing, and interpersonal skills. \n• Proficiency in English and Chinese. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up- to-date curriculum vitae to Ms . Beatrice Wong ( bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ . All applications will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 20 November 2025 or until the position is filled.   "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CSC/2026/Aug/csc_it_ft_2026-08-26.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Audio Visual (AV) / IT Technician",
      "description": "HONG KONG SHUE YAN UNIVERSITY \nComputing Services Centre \n \nPosition: Audio Visual (AV) / IT Technician \nMajor Responsibilities: \n• Provide frontline Audio Visual (AV) and IT support for  staff and students under the \nUser Services Section, ensuring smooth daily operations within the Computing \nServices Centre and across the University. \n• Manage and support AV facilities in classrooms and lecture halls, ensuring the smooth \noperation, maintenance, and troubleshooting of AV hardware and software for teaching \nand learning activities. \n• Liaise with vendors for equipment maintenance and repairs , inventory control, and \nconduct routine inspection and maintenance of AV equipment including setup, \ntroubleshooting, and support for teaching, conferences, meetings, and special events. \n• Deliver on-site AV and IT support for University events and activities. \n• Maintain and update user guides, operation manuals, knowledge base articles, and other \nIT-related documentation. \n• Perform other tasks as assigned. \n \nRequirements: \n• Diploma or above in Multimedia Technology, I T, Computer Science, or a related \ndiscipline from a recognized University, College, or Technical Institute. \n• Minimum of 2 years of relevant experience in AV support, IT support, or a related field. \n• Hands-on experience with Zoom, Teams, and control systems. \n• Good knowledge of PC hardware, software, and troubleshooting techniques. \n• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. \n• Good interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. \n• Good command of both spoken and written English and Chinese. \n \nSalary will be commensurate with qualification and experience. Candidates with more \nexperience will be considered as Senior IT Technician. \n \nThe appointment is contract-based and renewable upon mutual agreement. Applicants should \napply by sending a completed application form, resume and Cover Letter via email to \ncscjob@hksyu.edu. \n \nDeadline: The posts are open until filled. \nPlease complete the application form via the hyperlink below: \nhttps://eform2.hksyu.edu/view.php?id=15970 \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data received will be used for recruitment \npurposes only. Applications will receive full consideration until the positions are filled.  "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2025/Oct/rcdtbi_AI_programmer_ft_2025-10-30.pdf": {
      "title": "We are hiring an  AI Programmer  for the QESS project “Developing an AI -Enhanced Teaching",
      "description": "Full-time AI Programmer  \nWe are hiring an  AI Programmer  for the QESS project “Developing an AI -Enhanced Teaching \nResource Hub for the Self-Financing Higher Education Sector” under the Research Center for Digital \nEducation and Blended Intelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. This inter-institutional project \naims to centralize and utilize AI learning resources and tools to support teaching and the development \nof AI literacy among post-secondary teachers across four self-financing higher education institutions, \nprovide effective AI tools for teaching in self -financing institutions, organize professional \ndevelopment activities, and conduct research to evaluate AI literacy initiatives. \nThe AI Programmer will develop, integrate, and maintain educational AI tools and features for the AI-\nEnhanced Teaching Resource Hub, working closely with faculty, internal tech teams, and other project \nstaff. \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n• Develop and integrate advanced AI features into the Teaching Resource Hub. \n• Customize educational AI tools for specific subject content and teaching needs. \n• Ensure the platform’s functionality, scalability, security, and smooth integration of AI tools. \n• Troubleshoot technical issues and implement updates based on user feedback and analytics. \n• Conduct testing and quality assurance for all AI tools and platform features. \n• Collaborate with technical vendors and the internal tech team to support platform and AI tool \ndevelopment. \n• Support the development and implementation of ethical guidelines for AI usage within the \nplatform. \nQualifications and Requirements \n• A Bachelor’s degree or above in Computer Science, Information Technology, Data Science, or a \nrelated field. \n• Experience in AI development, programming, or educational technology preferred. \n• Proficiency in programming languages and AI frameworks relevant to platform development. \n• Strong problem-solving, analytical, and communication skills. \n• Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n• Interest in applying AI to enhance teaching and learning in higher education. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up- to-date curriculum vitae to Ms . Beatrice Wong ( bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ . All applications will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 20 November 2025 or until the position is filled.   \n \n  \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SW/2026/May/sw_ra_pt_2026-05-28.pdf": {
      "title": "Department of Social Work: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months)",
      "description": "Department of Social Work: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months)  \nJob duties:  \nThe RA will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) to conduct research project entitled “Exploring the role \nof social capital in community-based sharing: The case of community living room (URG/25/08)”, which is \nfunded by the Hong Kong Shue Yan University’s University Research Fund. The appointee will be \nresponsible for the following tasks:  \na. Assisting with literature review \nb. Liaising with research collaborators and partners \nc. Conducting interviews \nd. Draft research report \ne. Other assigned duties \n \nRequirements:  \nApplicants should have: A bachelor degree in social sciences or a related discipline (preferred). \nKnolwedge in qualitative research methods. Proficiency in computer software applications. Ability to \nwork independently and collaboratively. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English and \nChinese. The appointment will be made on the basis of a one-year contract, with a possibility of \nrenewal, subject to mutual agreement and funding availability. The remuneration package will be \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication:  \nApplicants should submit a completed application form along with a CV to Dr. Lai Ka Wai (Principal \nInvestigator) at mkwlai@hksyu.edu. \n \nApplication Forms (academic positions) can be obtained at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy. All application materials will be treated in strict \nconfidence. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/CIEBPR/2026/May/ciebpr_cpsy_ft_2026-05-08.pdf": {
      "title": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice",
      "description": "Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice \nand Research \n \nHong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) \n \nCounselling Psychologist \n \nThe Hong Kong Shue Yan University (HKSYU) is seeking high-calibre candidates to join the Mrs \nDorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for Interdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice and \nResearch. The Centre hosts a community project that aspires to strengthen the social-emotional \ncapabilities of students and their parents, teachers, social workers, and the public.  The project \nincorporates gamification elements into social-emotional learning programmes for Primary 3 and 4 \nstudents. \n \nResponsibilities: \n• Design integrative and gamified emotional learning materials tailored social emotional learning \n• Provide consultation services to students, parents, and teachers participating in the project \n• Deliver outreach psycho-educational/ consultation service to schools \n• Assist in conducting research-related tasks, including data collection, analysis and report \nwriting etc. \n• Assist in the development and execution of publicity events related \n• Assist in drafting progress reports and evaluation studies as required by project manager \n• Any other responsibilities as assigned by the Centre Directors  \n \nRequirements: \n• Master’s degree in Counselling Psychology and Registered Counselling Psychologist of the \n“Hong Kong Psychological Society” preferred \n• Three years or above of counselling experience in an educational or related setting \n• Proficiency in SPSS, along with experience in both quantitative and qualitative data collection \nand analysis \n• Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively in a team environment \n• Proficiency in spoken and written English and Chinese \n \nApplication: \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover \nletter and an updated curriculum vitae, to the Mrs Dorothy Koo and Dr Ti-Hua Koo Centre for \nInterdisciplinary Evidence-based Practice & Research (ciebpr@hksyu.edu). \n \nApplication form (research positions) can be downloaded \nat: https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/ \n \nAll applications will be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be \ncontacted. \n \nClosing Date: 25 May or until the positions are filled, whichever is earlier. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/EF/2026/Jan/ef_ra_ft_pt_2026-01-19.pdf": {
      "title": "project team now seeks to appoint a passionate candidate for the position of Research",
      "description": "Supported by the Faculty Development Scheme (FDS) 2025/26 Exercise, Research Grants \nCouncil with reference no. UGC/FDS15/B01/25, a project team from the Department of \nEconomics and Finance, Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct a two-year research \nproject entitled “Examining Impacts of Channel Addition/Elimination on Perceived Control \nand Concern about Cybersecurity: A Scenario-based Survey Study of Virtual Banking”. The \nproject team now seeks to appoint a passionate candidate for the position of Research \nAssistant (Full-time / Part-time) for the project. \n \nResearch Assistant (Full-time / Part-time) \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be: \n• Conduct literature review, data collection and data analysis \n• Assist in the compilation of research reports and other forms of deliverables \n• Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should possess: \n• Preferably a bachelor’s degree with some quantitative research experience \n• Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese \n• Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines \n \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Jan 2026 to 31st December 2026. The remuneration \npackage will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae to the Principal Investigator of the project Dr LEE Tin Yun Philip \n[tylee@hksyu.edu]. Application form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy  \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely \nfor recruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment \nexercise. \n \nDeadline \nUntil the position is filled. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Aug/counpsy_ra_pt_2026-08-28.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Part-time Research Assistant",
      "description": "Position: Part-time Research Assistant \nSupported by the Faculty Development Scheme (FDS), Research Grants Council \n(UGC/FDS15/H13/25), a project team from  the Department of Counselling and \nPsychology at Hong Kong Shue Yan University is conducting a research project entitled  \n“Enhancing Compassion, Help -seeking Intention and Mental Wellbeing of Emerging \nAdults with ACEs through a Compassion-based Intervention” . The project team is seeking \na passionate candidate for the position of Research Assistant (Part-time) for the project. \n \nMajor Responsibilities  \n• Liaising with different parties for data collection and project implementation \n• Prepare research materials and facilitate group sessions with study protocols. \n• Collecting, entering, processing, and analysing data \n• Assist in the compilation of research reports and other forms of deliverables \n• Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team \n \nRequirements  \nApplicants should possess:  \n• A Bachelor’s degree or above in counselling, psychology, social work, or related \ndisciplines \n• Relevant experience in qualitative and quantitative research \n• Experience in leading mindfulness- or compassion -based groups, and/or \nfacilitating psychoeducational group sessions \n• Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese \n• Strong organizational and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work \nindependently and manage multiple tasks effectively \n• Proficient computer skills and data analysis software (e.g. MS Office, SPSS) \n \nThe Appointment commences as soon as possible  for a duration of 6 months . The \nremuneration package will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  \n \nApplication  \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae with the expected salary to Dr. Winnie Yuen ( Principal Investigator) at \nwyyuen@hksyu.edu.  Application form can be obtained at:  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used \nsolely for recruitment -related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the \nrecruitment exercise.  \n \nClosing Date \n7 September 2026 "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Jul/counpsy_lab_asst_m_ft_2026-07-09.pdf": {
      "title": "Job Title: Lab Assistant [1 position] and Lab Manager [1 position]",
      "description": "Job Title: Lab Assistant [1 position] and Lab Manager [1 position] \nMode: Full-time \nAppointment Period: 12-24 months with the possibility of renewal subject to mutual agreement \nDepartment: Department of Counselling & Psychology- Neuro and Cyber Forensic Psychology \nLaboratory (NCFPL) \nClosing Date: September 30th 2026 \n \n(1) Lab Assistant  \nJob Duties \nThe appointee will be responsible for (a) conducting quantitative and qualitative research studies, \nincluding research design, data collection, analysis, compilation of reports and other \nforms of deliverables; (b) providing administrative support to the laboratory manager and directors; \n(c) Preparing literature review regarding neuroscience and forensic psychology; (d) compiling \nprogress reports and the final report; e) assisting the publications and other related research work in \nthe laboratory; f) maintaining laboratory equipment and ensure compliance with safety protocols; and \ng) assisting with course tutorials and preparation. Supportive supervision will be provided upon \nappointment. \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should have \n(a) bachelor’s degree in Psychology or a related field; \n(b) excellent command of SPSS; \n(c) good skills in psychology- related data collection; \n(d) excellent command of English and Chinese language (Cantonese); \n(e) personal quality of good responsibility, industriousness and readiness to learn and to help other \npeople. \n \n(2) Lab Manager \nJob Duties \nThe appointee will be responsible for (a) overseeing daily laboratory operations and ensuring \ncompliance with safety regulations; (b) managing budgets, resources, and inventory of laboratory \nsupplies and equipment; (c) coordinating research projects, including planning, execution, and data \nanalysis; (d) supervising and training lab assistant and interns, providing mentorship and guidance; (e) \nfacilitating collaboration among researchers and external partners; and f) assisting with course \ntutorials and preparation. \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should have \n(a) master’s degree or PhD in Psychology, Neuroscience, or a related field; \n(b) experience in laboratory management and research coordination; \n(c) excellent command of SPSS and familiarity with research methodologies and data analysis \ntechniques; \n(d) strong leadership skills with the ability to mentor and motivate staff; \n(e) excellent organizational and communication skills. \nFunding information \nSalary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter, and a curriculum \nvitae (CV) to: Prof. Edmond Lau and Dr. Bess Lam at Email kllau@hksyu.edu and \nyhlam@hksyu.edu with the subject “application for lab assistant or lab manager”. It would be nice if \nthe applicant could also attach to the email a sample of his or her university assignments or research \npapers that can demonstrate his or her proficiency in English writing. \n \nApplication forms can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/tc/about/career/ \nAll applicants will be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Mar/counpsy_ra_2026-03-05.pdf": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Full Time/ Part Time)",
      "description": "Research Assistant (Full Time/ Part Time) \nDepartment of Counselling and Psychology \nThe appointee will work on a project named “Provision of Services for Basic, Advanced and/or Thematic \nCourses for Teacher Professional Development on Catering for Students with Special Educational Needs \nfor the 2024/25, 2025/26 and 2026/27 School Years”. \nResponsibilities \n• Assisting in implementing research projects under the supervision of the Program coordinator \nand Project Manager, including literature review, data collection, entry, processing and analysis, \ndraft report and other research duties assigned. \n• Providing programme and secretariat support \n• Liaising with internal and external parties \n• Organizing events/functions/visits \n• System work and office management \n• Performing any other duties as assigned \nRequirements \n• Bachelor's degree \n• Preferably with several years of post-qualification working experience \n• Have good interpersonal and communication skills \n• Proficiency in both spoken and written English and Chinese \n• Literary in computer applications \n• Self-motivated and able to work independently or as a team member \nImmediate availability is preferred. \nFor enquiries, please contact Ms. Twinkle Lam via e-mail: sclam@hksyu.edu \n \nApplication Procedure \nApplicants should send a letter of application together with curriculum vitae to the following address or \nby email: \nMs. Twinkle Lam \nDepartment of Counselling & Psychology \nHong Kong Shue Yan University, \n10 Wai Tsui Crescent, \nBraemar Hill, Hong Kong \nE-mail: sclam@hksyu.edu \nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Personal data collected will be used for staff recruitment \npurposes only. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2026/Mar/counpsy_ra_pt_2026-03-02.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Part-time Research Assistant",
      "description": "Position: Part-time Research Assistant \nJob Duties \nThe part-time RA will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) to conduct research project \nentitled  “ Efficacy of a mindfulness -based intervention with and without virtual reality \nsupport to promote mental health through self-compassion and mind wandering among \nuniversity students: A randomised controlled trial  (URG/24/07)” , which is funded by the \nHong Kong Shue Yan University’s University Research Fund. \n \nMajor Responsibilities  \n• Collecting, entering, processing, and analysing data \n• Liaising with different parties for data collection \n• Assist in group sessions \n• Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the PI to support \nthe operation of the research project \n \nRequirements  \nApplicants should possess:  \n• Bachelor’s degree in counselling, psychology, social work, or related disciplines \n• Preferably with both qualitative and quantitative research experience \n• Preferably with experience in mindfulness and/or facilitating group sessions \n• Strong command of written and spoken English and Chinese \n• Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently, and capable of meeting tight \ndeadlines \n• Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills \n• Proficient computer skills, including MS Office applications and SPSS \n \nThe Appointment commences as soon as possible  to 30 June 2026. The remuneration \npackage will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  \n \nApplication  \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae with the expected salary to Dr. Winnie Yuen (the PI)  at \nwyyuen@hksyu.edu.  Application form can be obtained at:  \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used \nsolely for recruitment -related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the \nrecruitment exercise.  \n \nClosing Date \nUntil the position is filled. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/counpsy/2025/Dec/counpsy_ra_ft_2025-12-23.pdf": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Full-time, 4-month Fixed Contract)",
      "description": " \n \nResearch Assistant (Full-time, 4-month Fixed Contract) \nProject Title: \nVirtual Reality–Based Cognitive Behavioral Therapy for Social Anxiety–Driven \nDepression among Youths: A Randomized Controlled Trial (UGC/FDS15/H14/24) 基\n於虛擬現實的認知行為治療對社交焦慮型抑鬱青少年的效果研究：一項隨機對\n照實驗 \n \nJob Responsibilities \n• Support the implementation of a VR-based psychological intervention for \nyouths with social anxiety and depression. \n• Work closely with the project team and liaise with different stakeholders, \nincluding schools, NGOs, and research staff. \n• Assist with participant recruitment, intervention delivery, data collection, and \nfollow-up arrangements. \n• Carry out other research and administrative tasks as assigned by the team \nleader. \nRequirements \n• Registered counseling psychologist or holder of a related professional \nqualification. \n• Familiar with Cognitive Behavioral Therapy. \n• Able to work independently and take initiative. \n• Self-motivated, responsible, and able to work well in a team. \n• Strong interpersonal and communication skills. \n• Able to fully commit to the project from Monday to Friday; occasional work \noutside regular working hours may be required, depending on project needs. \n• Fluent in Chinese and English (Cantonese, Mandarin, and English). \nThis role is quite intensive, but it offers an excellent opportunity to quickly \naccumulate around 300 hours of direct counseling practice. Applicants should \nhave strong time management skills, be able to work well under pressure, and \ndemonstrate a high degree of flexibility. \nPreferred Qualifications \n \n \n• Experience working with children or adolescents. \n• Interest in or familiarity with technology-assisted interventions, such as VR. \n• Able to start work as soon as possible. \nWhat You Will Gain \n• Substantial clinical exposure through direct involvement in intervention \ndelivery. \n• Hands-on experience in research implementation, data collection, and \nteamwork. \n• Strong preparation for future research postgraduate applications or advanced \nclinical training. \nAppointment Details \n• Contract period: 4 months (initially), with the possibility of extension \ndepending on project progress and mutual agreement \n• Salary: HKD 21,000 per month (fixed) \n• Closing date: Until the position is filled \nApplication Method \nInterested applicants should send: \n1. A completed application form (including job expectation) \n2. An updated CV \nto Dr. WANG Yi-Zhou Joe by email: ywang@hksyu.edu "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SOC/2026/Aug/soc_ra_pt_2026-08-03.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Part-time Research",
      "description": "Department of Sociology  \nPosition: Part-time Research \nAssistant \n \n \nJob Duties \nThe appointee will assist in implementing a URG funded project entitled “Playing with the \nPast: The Heritage Management Board Game as a Mediating Site for Critical and Innovative \nHeritage Learning” undertaken by Dr. XIE Jieyi from the Department of Sociology. \n \nThey will be responsible for the following tasks:  \n(a) literature review; \n(b) data collection and data entry; \n(c) drafting research report; and \n(d) other research and administrative duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator. \n \nRequirements  \nApplicants should have: (i) preferably a master’s degree in anthropology, sociology, cultural \nstudy, media study or related disciplines;  (ii) proficiency in qualitative data processing \napplication (iii) ability to work independently and collaboratively; and (iv) good written and \noral communication skills in English, Cantonese, and Putonghua. \n \nTerms and Conditions \nThe appointment will be made on the basis of a one-year contract, with a possibility of renewal, \nsubject to mutual agreement and funding availability.  \n \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae with expected salary to jxie@hksyu.edu. Application form (academic \npositions) can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications \nwill be treated in strict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted. \n \n \n \nClosing Date: 11/09/2026 "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SOC/2026/Mar/soc_ra_pt_2026-03-23.pdf": {
      "title": "Part -time Research Assistant in EEG -Driven VR Systems for Emotional Regulation",
      "description": "Part -time Research Assistant in EEG -Driven VR Systems for Emotional Regulation \nResearch  (Ref: URG/ 25/06) \nPosition: Part-time Research Assistant (Start date: May 2026) \nProject Details:  MindScapes: EEG-Driven Virtual Reality for Emotional Regulation and \nUser-Centric Testing \nThis research project investigates the integration of real-time EEG biofeedback with \nimmersive VR environments to support emotional regulation and mental well-being. \nThe study focuses on developing and validating an accessible, user-centered system \nthat combines art therapy principles, meditation techniques, and culturally-inspired \nspatial design. Through structured user testing, the project aims to refine the system's \nadaptive feedback mechanisms and evaluate its effectiveness in promoting emotional \nrelief and self-awareness. (PI: Miss Xinzhou ZHANG) \n \nKey Responsibilities:  \nThe appointee will assist the Principal Investigator in the following tasks: \n• Organizing and coordinating user testing sessions, including participant scheduling \nand venue setup \n• Recording and documenting user interactions during VR testing sessions \n• Collecting and organizing quantitative data (EEG metrics, engagement duration, \nsystem performance) \n• Assisting with the administration and collection of questionnaires and feedback forms \n• Transcribing and organizing qualitative data from semi-structured interviews \n• Maintaining organized databases of user testing results and feedback \n• Supporting prototype iteration and debugging processes when needed \n• Assisting with preliminary data analysis and visualization \n• Contributing to the preparation of research documentation and reports \n \nRequirements:  \n• A bachelor's degree or current enrollment in a program related to Psychology, \nSociology, Human-Computer Interaction, Digital Media, Computer Science, or related \ndisciplines \n• Strong organizational skills and attention to detail in data collection and management \n• Basic familiarity with VR technology and user experience testing (training will be \nprovided) \n• Excellent interpersonal skills for participant interaction and coordination \n• Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese/Putonghua) \n• Experience with data entry and basic statistical software (e.g., Excel, SPSS) is an \nadvantage \n• Interest in mental health, meditation, or emotional well-being research is preferred \n• Ability to work independently and maintain confidentiality of research data \n \nTerms of Appointment:  \n• The appointment is on a part-time basis (approximately 10-15 hours per week during \ntesting phases, totaling 70 hours over the project period) \n• Working hours will be flexible but may include some weekends to accommodate \nparticipant availability \n• Remuneration: HK$100 per hour \n• Duration: June 2026 - September 2026 (approximately 3 months) \n \nApplication Procedure:  \nInterested candidates should send a cover letter and CV to Miss Xinzhou ZHANG via \nemail at [xzzhang@hksyu.edu] by April 30. \nReview of applications will commence immediately and continue until the position is \nfilled. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview. \nThe University reserves the right not to fill this position or to fill the position by invitation. \nPersonal data provided by applicants will be used for recruitment purposes only. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/EF/2025/Nov/ef_ra_pt_ft_2025-11-04.pdf": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Full-time / Part-time)",
      "description": "Supported by the Faculty Development Scheme (FDS) 2025/26 Exercise, Research Grants Council \nwith reference no. UGC/FDS15/E04/25, a project team from the Department of Economics and \nFinance, Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct a two-year research project entitled “A Green \nStructural Efficiency Framework for New Quality Productive Forces” . The project team now seeks \nto appoint a high-calibre candidate for the position of Research Assistant (Full-time / Part-time) for \nthe project.  \nResearch Assistant (Full-time / Part-time) \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be:  \n• Conduct literature review, data collection and data analysis \n• Assist in the compilation of research reports and other forms of deliverables \n• Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team \nRequirements  \nApplicants should possess:  \n• A bachelor’s degree, preferably with some quantitative research experience \n• Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese \n• Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Jan 2026 to 31st December 2027. The remuneration package \nwill be commensurate with qualiﬁcations and experience.  \nApplication  \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a curriculum \nvitae to the Principal Investigator of the project Dr TSANG Chun-kei [cktsang@hksyu.edu]. \nApplication form can be obtained at: https://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy  \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise.  \nDeadline  \nUntil the position is ﬁlled. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2026/Jul/rcdebi_ra_ft_2026-07-15.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-Time Research Assistant",
      "description": "Full-Time Research Assistant \nWe are hiring a Research Assistant   under the Research Center for Digital Education and Blended \nIntelligence, Hong Kong Shue Yan University. The Research Assistant will support research related \nto digital pedagogy and well-being.  \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n• Conduct literature reviews and synthesize research on digital pedagogy, blended intelligence, and \nwell-being. \n• Assist in designing research instruments and coordinating data collection activities (surveys, \ninterviews, and focus groups). \n• Perform quantitative and qualitative data analysis and manage project databases. \n• Support the implementation, testing, and user-support of digital learning platforms and well-\nbeing tools. \n• Assist in drafting research ethics applications, progress reports, grant proposals, and academic \nmanuscripts. \n• Coordinate communication between the Research Center, investigators, school partners, and \nstakeholders. \n• Assist in organizing academic seminars, workshops, and knowledge transfer events. \n• Handle day-to-day project administration, including tracking timelines, maintaining records, and \nscheduling meetings. \nQualifications and Requirements \n• A Bachelor’s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, or a related discipline. \n• Experience in research, data collection, and analysis preferred. \n• Proficiency in data analysis software (SPSS, Mplus, R) is an advantage. \n• Strong organizational, writing, analytical, and interpersonal skills. \n• Proficiency in English and Chinese. \n• Interest in educational research and supporting teaching innovation through AI. \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Dr Jason CHOW (tschow@hksyu.edu) . The Application form \ncan be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in strict \nconfidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted.  \nClosing Date: by 10 August 2026 or until the position is filled.   \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/RCDTBI/2026/Feb/rcdtbi_ra_ft_2026-02-12.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-Time Research Assistant",
      "description": "Full-Time Research Assistant \nWe are hiring a Research Assistant under the Research Center for Digital Education and Blended \nIntelligence, Hong Kong Shue Y an University. This position supports projects that identify, centralize, \nand utilize digital technologies and tools to enhance mental health support and learning outcomes. The \nrole involves conducting research to evaluate digital teaching and mental health programs, designing \neffective digital tools for mental health and learning, and organizing professional development \nactivities.  \nMajor Duties and Responsibilities \n• Assist in conducting research on digital technologies for mental health and learning support, \nincluding survey studies, focus groups, and public data analysis.  \n• Collaborate with faculty members and subject matter experts to document digitally enhanced \nshowcases for mental health and learning.  \n• Conduct literature reviews and compile data on best practices for integrating digital technologies \nin mental health support and learning.  \n• Analyze user feedback, platform data, and research findings to evaluate project’s effectiveness. \n• Assist in organizing and documenting workshops, seminars, and conference.  \n• Assist in writing research reports and disseminate findings through online platforms, seminars, and \npublications. \n \nQualifications and Requirements \n• A Bachelor’s degree or above in Psychology, Education, Social Sciences, or a related discipline.  \n• Experience in academic research in psychology, education, and related fields.   \n• Proficiency in quantitative data analysis software (SPSS; Mplus or R). \n• Strong organizational, writing, analytical, and interpersonal skills. \n• Proficiency in English and Chinese.  \n \nApplication \nApplicants should send a completed application form with expected salary, together with a cover letter \nand an up-to-date curriculum vitae to Ms. Beatrice Wong (bkywong@hksyu.edu). The Application \nform can be downloaded at https://www.hksyu.edu/en/about/career/. All applications will be treated in \nstrict confidence. Only those who are shortlisted will be contacted. \nClosing Date: Until the position is filled. "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/JC/2025/Oct/jc_ra_pt_2025-10-13.pdf": {
      "title": "qualified candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project.",
      "description": "Supported by the Research Grants Council Faculty Development Scheme [reference no. \nUGC/FDS15/B02/23], the Department of Journalism and Communication, Hong Kong Shue Yan \nUniversity has been conducting the research project entitled “Does Corporate Sociopolitical Activism \nOriented Market Exits Benefit Corporate Brand Equity and Firm Profitability? Evidence from Corporate \nExodus from Russia amidst the 2022 Russo-Ukrainian War”. The Department is seeking to appoint a \nqualified candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project. \n \nPost: Part-time Research Assistant \nThe appointee will be responsible for: \n• Assisting in data analysis; \n• Preparing publicity materials; \n• Provide assistance in conducting literature review \n• Compiling project completion report; and \n• Conducting other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team. \n \nRequirements \nApplicants should possess: \n• A Master’s degree or above in social sciences, preferably with experience in conducting \nresearch projects; \n• Proficiency in statistical analysis \n• Good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese; \n• Self-motivated and strong sense of responsibility  \n• Good command of interpersonal communication skills \n• Immediate availability is highly preferred; \n \nThe Appointment commences on 20th Oct 2025 to 31st December 2025. The remuneration package will \nbe commensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a curriculum vitae to Dr. ZHANG \nXiao, Grace at xzhang@hksyu.edu  \n \nApplication form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \nApplicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within \ntwo months of application. \n \nDeadline: \nUntil position is filled. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/ACC/2025/Jun/acc_ra_pt_2025-06-13.pdf": {
      "title": "Department of Accounting: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months",
      "description": "Department of Accounting: Part-time Research Assistant (One Position for 12 months \nwith possibility of extension)   \nJob duties: The RA will assist the Principal Investigator (PI) to conduct research project \nproject entitled “The Impact of Tax Enforcement on Corporate Tax Avoidance During Covid-\n19 and Beyond (URG/24/19)”, which is funded by the Hong Kong Shue Yan University’s \nUniversity Research Fund.   \nThe appointee will be responsible for the following tasks:   \na. Manually collecting data, entering, processing, and analyzing data;  \nb. Providing support in the literature review, data management, and data analysis;   \nc. Making phone calls for data collection, liaising with different parties for data collection;   \nd. Performing any other administrative duties as assigned by the PI to support the operation \nof the research project.   \nRequirements:   \nApplicants should have:   \ni. A Master’s degree (or above) in Accounting/Finance or a related field, PhD \ndegree holder is preferred;  \nii. Strong background in qualitative and computational research methods; \niii. Good interpersonal and communication skills (proficiency in English and \nGood written skills in English and Chinese);   \niv. Exhibit a positive attitude, self-motivation, and have an ability to work \nindependently and collaboratively   \nv. Be willing to learn new concepts related to business applications  \n \nTerms and conditions:   \nThe appointment will be made on the basis of a one-year contract, with a possibility of \nrenewal, subject to mutual agreement and funding availability. The remuneration package \nwill be commensurate with qualifications and experience.   \nApplication:   \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae with the expected salary to Dr. Vivian Wang (the PI) at vxwang@hksyu.edu. \nApplication Forms (academic positions) can be obtained at \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy. All application materials will be treated \nin strict confidence. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted.   \nClosing Date: Applications will be reviewed as received until the post is filled.  "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/JC/2023/Aug/jc_ra_pt_2023-08-16.pdf": {
      "title": "calibre candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project.",
      "description": "Supported by the Chinese Heritage Research Grant (CHRG) with the reference no. CHRG/22/04, the \nDepartment of Journalism and Communication, Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct the one-\nyear research project entitled “Our Fading Folk Games: Revitalization and Inheritance of Chinese \nHeritage Games in Immersive Virtual Environments”. The Department now seeks to appoint a high \ncalibre candidate to the position of Part-time Research Assistant for the project. \n \nResearch Assistant \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be: \n• Conducting Literature review, data collection and data analysis; \n• Liaison with participants; \n• Assist in project events; \n• Assist in the compilation of research reports and other forms of deliverables; \n• Assist in building virtual environments; \n• Compiling project final report; and \n• Other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team. \n \nRequirements \n \nApplicants should possess: \n• A Bachelor’s degree, preferably with some research/ project management experience; \n• Proficiency in Unity and Blender engines; \n• Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese; \n• Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines; \n• Immediate availability is highly preferred; \n \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Sep 2023 to 31st Aug 2024. The remuneration package will be \ncommensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a curriculum vitae \nto Dr. Kung Wong, LAU [laukw@hksyu.edu]. \n \nApplication form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purpose. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \nDeadline \nUntil position is filled. \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/SOC/2023/Apr/chrg_ra_2023-04-27_pt.pdf": {
      "title": "Position: Parttime Research Assistant",
      "description": "Position: Parttime Research Assistant \n \nThe appointee will work for a CHRG (Chinese Heritage Research Grant) funded project \non developing a comprehensive examination of Cantonese Collectors in Shanghai. \n \nSelected candidates are requiredto: \n \n provide professional assistance to the project leader and project team; \n plan, supervise, coordinate and execute the various professional activities of the \nleader's learning plan; and \n perform other tasks as assigned. \n \nCandidates should possess:  \n a higher diploma or university degree in history, art history, cultural studies or \nrelated disciplines in the humanities;  \n have good interpersonal and organizational skills;  \n practical experience in provision of support services to users; \n good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese;  \n good computer skills, e.g. MS Office applications; and  \n having work experience in the higher education sector will be an advantage.  \n \nApplicants should email Application Form, Resume and Cover Letter to Dr NG Ni Na \nCamellia at nnng@hksyu.edu. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and \nexperience. The initial appointment will be for a period of 6 months with the \npossibility of renewal subject to mutual agreement. \n \nThe application form can be accessed at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/Application%20Form%20for%20non-\nAcademic%20Positions.doc \n \nAll application materials will be held in strict confidence. Only those who are short-\nlisted will be contacted. The application will be closed when the post is filled. \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.hksyu.edu/assets/careers/ADSCI/2024/Nov/adsci_ra_ft_2024-11-15.pdf": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Supported by the Faculty Development Scheme (FDS) 2024/25 Exercise, Research Grants \nCouncil with reference no. UGC/FDS15/H16/24, Prof Kung Wong, LAU from the Department \nof Applied Data Science , Hong Kong Shue Yan University will conduct a two -year research \nproject entitled “Understanding the Elderly-computer Interaction (ECI) in Social-Virtual Reality \nApplications: An Exploratory Study of the Semiotic-driven Approach and Post-experiment User \nEnquiry”. The Department now seeks to appoint a high-calibre candidate for the position of Full-\ntime Research Assistant for the project.  The primary responsibilities will include assisting the \nPrincipal Investigator (PI) in setting up the Virtual Reality (VR) instrument, conducting research \ndesign, and collecting and analyzing data during experiments, surveys, and other documentary \ntasks. \n \nResearch Assistant \nThe major responsibilities of the appointee will be: \n• Assist in building virtual environments and platforms \n• Liaise with participants \n• Support project events \n• Compile research reports and other deliverables \n• Prepare the final project report \n• Perform other research and administrative duties as assigned by the project team. \n \nRequirements \n \nApplicants should possess: \n• A Bachelor’s degree, preferably with some research/ project management experience; \n• Proficiency in Unity, Unreal and/or Blender engines; \n• Good command of both written and spoken English, Chinese; \n• Mature, self-motivated, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines; \n \nThe Appointment commences on 1st Jan 2025 to 31st December 2026. The remuneration \npackage will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. \n \nApplication \n \nApplicants should send a completed application form, together with a cover letter and a \ncurriculum vitae to Ms. Eunice Leung [yyleung@hksyu.edu].  \n \nApplication form can be obtained at: \nhttps://www.hksyu.edu/en/snippets/external-vacancy \n \nOnly shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The information provided will be used solely for \nrecruitment-related purposes. All applications will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. \n \nDeadline \nUntil the position is filled. \n "
    }
  },
